flowchart TB
    accTitle: SyncStream change-data-capture architecture
    accDescr: PostgreSQL changes flow through Debezium and Kafka to independent Java product projectors for Redis and Elasticsearch. Each projector applies bounded retries and attempts to publish terminal failures to its dead-letter topic. This overview focuses on the core data plane.

    subgraph Capture["Change capture"]
        direction LR
        Postgres[("PostgreSQL / logical WAL")]
        Debezium["Debezium / Kafka Connect"]
        Kafka[("Kafka product events")]
        Postgres -->|"initial snapshot + row changes"| Debezium
        Debezium -->|"CDC envelopes"| Kafka
    end

    subgraph Projection["Independent product projections"]
        RedisConsumer["Java Redis projector + retry"]
        SearchConsumer["Java search projector + retry"]
        Redis[("Redis product cache")]
        Search[("Elasticsearch product index")]
        DLQ[("Per-consumer dead-letter topics")]
        RedisConsumer -->|"set / delete by ID"| Redis
        SearchConsumer -->|"upsert / delete by ID"| Search
        RedisConsumer -->|"failed event"| DLQ
        SearchConsumer -->|"failed event"| DLQ
    end

    Kafka -->|"consumer group A"| RedisConsumer
    Kafka -->|"consumer group B"| SearchConsumer
